    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169-a2">

                <pb facs="0301" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg295"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Cologan to the Chinese
                    Plenipotentiaries.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Highness, Excellency</hi>: In further reference to my
                    letter of the 29th of June, concerning the limits of the diplomatic quarter, I
                    have the honor to inform you that his excellency the minister of Great Britain,
                    no longer insisting on the destruction of the portion of the exterior wall of
                    the Imperial City situated to the north of his legation, the foreign
                    representatives have no objection to that wall being left standing.</p>
                <p>Agreement on the questions concerning the limits of the diplomatic quarter having
                    thus been reached, I beg your highness and your excellency to confirm this to me
                    in reply to my letter of the 29th of June.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
